Acceptance criteria for the fix
Two simultaneous requests for the same space and time slot must not both succeed.
Exactly one request must return 201 Created.
The other request must return 409 Conflict.
Only one booking must be created for the requested slot.
The conflicting request should identify the booking that caused the conflict, as required by the specification.
The Playwright concurrency regression test must pass after the defect is fixed.
Notes and suggested area

The issue appears to be related to concurrency handling during booking creation.

The defect was reproduced through API automation by sending two authenticated POST /api/bookings requests simultaneously using Promise.all().

The application currently allows both requests to receive 201 Created, indicating that the booking slot is not being protected correctly when simultaneous requests are processed.

Open question

The concurrency defect is confirmed through API testing.

The implementation should be investigated to determine why simultaneous requests can both successfully claim the same booking slot and ensure that the slot is protected against concurrent booking creation.